       "meta-title": "Post Purchase Survey Builder for Online Stores | Emergent",
       "meta-description": "Build a post purchase survey that asks where buyers found you, checks each delivery, and times reorder reminders. Free to start.",
       "name": "Build a Post Purchase Survey for the Moment After Checkout",
       "acrm---product-name": "Post Purchase Survey Builder",
       "description": "Get a post purchase survey that ties each answer to its order, from first-order source to fit and delivery problems.",
       "acrm---breadcrumb": "Post Purchase Survey",
       "explore-cta": "Build My Post Purchase Survey",
       "acrm---why-emergent-title": "Why Build Post Purchase Surveys With Emergent?",
       "awb---how-to-title": "How to Create a Post Purchase Survey",
       "awb---how-to-description": "Seven steps to plan a post purchase survey, build it with Emergent, and send each answer where it can act.",
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Post Purchase Survey FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a post purchase survey?\", \"a\": \"A post purchase survey is a short set of questions a buyer answers after placing an order, on the confirmation page or later by email or text. It asks what only the buyer knows at that point: where they heard of the store, whether the box arrived intact, how the product fits, and whether they plan to order again.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a post purchase survey?\", \"a\": \"Write one prompt for Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> that names the store, what you want to learn from buyers, and what should happen when an answer signals a problem. Emergent builds the survey with its database and dashboard, and the free tier covers building and publishing. Test it on one real order before the link goes live.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many post purchase survey questions should I ask?\", \"a\": \"Start with one to three on the confirmation page, and keep any follow-up email to five or fewer. Each question should feed a decision you will make. Cut any that would not. Once the first answers show what is missing, you can add a question by prompting Emergent again.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are some post purchase survey examples for an online store?\", \"a\": \"Three examples that go beyond order source and delivery: What almost stopped you from ordering today? Is this order a gift? Did you look at another store before buying? The gift and comparison questions work as a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/yes-no-questions'>yes no questions survey</a>, with one open follow-up for anyone who answers yes.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should I look for in post-purchase survey software?\", \"a\": \"Look for four things: the survey can appear on your confirmation page and in emails, each answer is saved with its order number, a problem answer can alert a person, and you can export the data. With Emergent, the survey is an app you build, and its responses sit in a database you own with no response cap.\"}, {\"q\": \"How soon after delivery should a post-purchase survey go out?\", \"a\": \"Send the delivery question within 24 hours of the box being marked delivered, while the unboxing is fresh. Questions about fit or how fast a product runs out can wait until the buyer has used it. Send one reminder about three days later to anyone who has not answered, then stop.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is it okay to add humor to a post-purchase survey?\", \"a\": \"Yes, if it suits the brand and stays out of the way of the answer. Borrow a line from a list of <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/funny-questions'>funny survey questions</a> for the thank-you screen or one answer option, but keep the question itself plain so the answers stay easy to count. A candle shop can sound warmer than a pharmacy.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I tie post-purchase survey answers to the order they came from?\", \"a\": \"Put the order number in the survey link, for example ?order=48213. Each answer then saves with the order it belongs to, even when the buyer opens the link on another device. From there, join each answer to that order's products and ship date, and filter the results by either one.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should post purchase surveys differ for first-time and repeat buyers?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Ask first-time buyers how they found the store, since that answer only matters once. Ask repeat buyers what brings them back or what they would like you to stock next, and skip the source question. Tag each response with the buyer's order count so the dashboard can split the two groups.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a post-purchase survey be just one question?\", \"a\": \"Yes. A single question with fixed options works much like <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/poll-questions'>poll questions</a>: quick to answer and easy to count. Pick the one whose answer changes a decision, such as where the buyer heard of the store, and add Other with a short text box for answers you did not list.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
       "alpb---prompt": "<p>Build a post purchase survey that collects every answer in a database I own.</p><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbPrompt = {\"default\": \"Build a post purchase survey that collects every answer in a database I own.\", \"chips\": [{\"label\": \"Order Source\", \"add\": \"Add an order source question that asks buyers how they found the store.\"}, {\"label\": \"Delivery Check\", \"add\": \"Add a delivery check that asks whether the box arrived complete, on time, and undamaged.\"}, {\"label\": \"Fit Feedback\", \"add\": \"Add fit feedback that asks whether the product runs small, true to size, or large.\"}, {\"label\": \"Reorder Timing\", \"add\": \"Add reorder timing that asks when the buyer will run out and emails a reminder then.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
